== navigation, geometry, hit testing
ok FirstChild, NextSibling: title cells, then the cells, row-major
ok every cell of this grid is shown
ok LastChild, PreviousSibling: the same backwards
ok a cell: CellRect in screen coordinates
ok a title cell: its rectangle
ok ElementProviderFromPoint: the cell under the point
ok a title cell under the point
ok the indicator: the grid
ok without titles: no column headers
ok and a title cell is not available
ok the first child is cell (0, 0)
ok titles back: the title cell answers again
== the row window
ok more records than rows: RowCount = VisibleRowCount
ok fewer than the records
ok row 0: the first row shown
ok scrolled to the end: row 0 names the record shown there
ok another record
ok the last row: the last record
ok navigation: the shown elements
ok a cell of a destroyed grid: not available
ok and no parent
== SelectionItem
ok the current cell is selected
ok another is not
ok Select
ok the dataset moved to its row
ok its column is selected
ok now it is selected
ok the former current cell is not
ok AddToSelection of the selected cell: nothing changes
ok of another: refused
ok RemoveFromSelection of the selected cell: refused (a selection is required)
ok of another: nothing changes
ok the selection container is the grid
ok a disabled grid: its cells are not enabled
ok and Select is refused
== Value
ok Value: the text the cell shows
ok an editable column: not read-only
ok SetValue
ok the record is in edit mode
ok of the cell's row
ok the field has the new text
ok and the cell shows it
ok cancelled: the old text
ok a read-only column: read-only
ok SetValue refused
ok the other column is not
ok a read-only grid: read-only
ok SetValue refused
ok and the dataset is untouched
== focus
ok the grid has the focus
ok the current cell has the keyboard focus
ok another has not
ok GetFocus: the current cell
ok SetFocus of a cell
ok it becomes the current cell
ok in its column
ok a title cell cannot take the focus
== lifetime of the grid's elements
ok the dataset closed: the cell is not available
ok and the grid has no rows
ok opened again: the cell answers
ok the grid destroyed: the cell is not available
ok every provider object of the grids is released
== the navigator and its buttons
ok control type ToolBar
ok AutomationId: the component name
ok children: the visible buttons, named by their hints
ok LastChild, PreviousSibling: the same backwards
ok automation ids: the button identifiers
ok ElementProviderFromPoint: the button under the point
ok one provider per button
ok a button: Button
ok FrameworkId
ok not keyboard focusable
ok a content element
ok the Invoke pattern
ok no other pattern
ok bounding rectangle: ButtonRect in screen coordinates
ok runtime id [UiaAppendRuntimeId, Ord of the button]
ok the parent is the navigator
ok the fragment root is the navigator
ok outside the buttons: the navigator
ok a line of Hints: its short part names the button
ok no line: the default hint
== enabled from the dataset's state
ok the first record
ok the last record
ok a middle record
ok editing
ok a disabled navigator
ok a disabled form
ok a closed dataset
ok an empty dataset
== Invoke
ok a disabled button: refused
ok Invoke
ok the click is posted, not made at once
ok handled: the button was clicked
ok OnClick as for a mouse click
ok Invoke of Delete
ok the confirmation is not asked inside the call
ok it is asked when the click is handled
ok cancelled: nothing deleted
ok Invoke of Last
ok the button became disabled before the click was handled: not clicked
== lifetime of the buttons
ok hidden buttons are not children
ok a hidden button is not available
ok a visible one still answers
ok shown again: it answers again
ok a button of a destroyed navigator: not available
ok and no parent
ok and no pattern
ok every provider object of the navigator is released
ok every provider object is released
